    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20051126.0037\n\nCAIRO, Nov. 26 , 2005 (Xinhua)\n\nXinhua Mideast news advisory -- Nov. 26\n\n\n\n\nThe following major international news stories from the Middle East region are scheduled to be covered or pursued by Xinhua News Agency on Saturday.\n\n-- NATO parliamentary forum on the Greater Middle East opens in Doha Saturday. It is to run for two days.\n\n-- Lebanese Prime Minister Fouad Seniora arrives in Amman to preside over the Jordanian-Lebanese joint committee meetings with his Jordanian counterpart Adnan Badran. He will also hold talks with top Jordanian officials on regional and international issues of common concern and bilateral relations.\n\n-- Some 242 candidates in 68 constituencies in Egypt's nine governorates are competing in the run-offs of the second phase of parliamentary elections.",
